<com:TContent ID="body" >

<h1>THyperLink</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.THyperLink" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>THyperLink</tt> displays a hyperlink on a page. It renders an <tt>&lt;a&gt;</tt>
element. <tt>NavigateUrl</tt> becomes the <tt>href</tt> attribute, and <tt>Target</tt>
becomes the <tt>target</tt> attribute.
</p>

<h2>What the link shows</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Three properties compete to fill the link, and the control picks one of them in order.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Condition</th><th>The link contains</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ImageUrl</tt> is set</td>
	<td>An image. <tt>Text</tt> becomes the alternate text of that image rather than the link text.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ImageUrl</tt> is empty and <tt>Text</tt> is set</td>
	<td>The text of <tt>Text</tt>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td>Both are empty</td>
	<td>The body content written between the control's tags.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:THyperLink NavigateUrl="?page=Home" Text="Home" /&gt;
&lt;com:THyperLink NavigateUrl="?page=Home"&gt;
  &lt;com:TImage ImageUrl="home.png" AlternateText="" /&gt; Home
&lt;/com:THyperLink&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>Styling the image</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>ImageStyle</tt> holds the style of the image the link renders, separately from the
style of the link itself. Three older properties set parts of that style and are now
deprecated, because the HTML attributes behind them are obsolete.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Deprecated property</th><th>Use instead</th></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageAlign</tt></td><td><tt>ImageStyle</tt>, with the CSS <tt>float</tt> or <tt>vertical-align</tt> declaration.</td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageHeight</tt></td><td><tt>ImageStyle.Height</tt>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><tt>ImageWidth</tt></td><td><tt>ImageStyle.Width</tt>.</td></tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
A link that posts back to the server rather than navigating is a
<a href="?page=Controls.LinkButton">TLinkButton</a>.
</p>
